work_reference_number/permit_reference_number/USRN against BODS
VehicleRef/VehicleJourneyRef through spatial-temporal road-segment
intersection; derive observed excess traversal and recovery. For grid,
preserve every twice-weekly TEC register and join Project
ID/site/Gate/capacity/date with DNO headroom and regulatory fee/milestone
state. For FHRS, ingest the free unauthenticated FSA API and explicitly
bridge FHRSID changes using LocalAuthorityBusinessID, normalized
name/address/postcode/geocode and council migration notices; enrich likely
corporate operators through Companies House only where identity confidence
is sufficient.

Plantability: Street Manager public API requires free registration; BODS
free consumer API key; NESO TEC is keyless open data and updates
Tuesday/Friday; FSA FHRS is free, no registration; Companies House API is
free with 600 requests/5 minutes; Planning Data is keyless and provides API
plus bulk CSV/JSON/GeoJSON/Parquet. Source costs are =C2=A30/month for all
proposed kernels.

Critical negative evidence: Planning Data says planning-application
specification is still in development and LPAs are not required to supply
it; do not treat absence as absence of applications. Generic static joins
are kill-gated because they can be rebuilt later. FHRS becomes interesting
only if we can prove identity continuity through ID churn and derive
economically useful site/operator lifecycle events; otherwise kill it as a
commodity ratings mirror.

Next probes: quantify BODS/Street Manager match coverage in one authority;
inspect existing Causeway predictive intervention capabilities; reconstruct
TEC transition tape; test 100 FHRS ID migrations against
name/address/geocode continuity and Companies House resolution; audit
